# What does not go into the build context (ERT-1220).

# The single most important line here. build/ is ~326 MB, of which build/logs
# alone is ~290 MB, and every byte of it would be shipped to the daemon on every
# image build for no purpose whatsoever.
build/
out/
.kotlin/
.amper/

.git/
.github/
.idea/
*.iml

# The PRD, the audits, the backlog. Nothing in the image reads them, and they
# churn constantly, which would invalidate a layer for a documentation edit.
docs/
*.md

# Inert for the application -- it reads System.getenv directly and there is no
# dotenv library on the classpath -- and must never enter an image regardless.
.env
.env.*

.DS_Store
*.log
.mcp.json
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# Excluded deliberately. The task graph is
#   executableJarJvm -> compileJvm, runtimeClasspathJvm
# with no test task in it, so `./kotlin package` does not compile tests -- and
# excluding them means a test-only commit does not invalidate the image build.
#
# IF THE BUILD FAILS WHILE LOADING THE PROJECT MODEL, delete the next line. That
# is the failure mode to expect (Amper reading module.yaml's test-dependencies
# and looking for the directory), and it is a model error, not a compile error.
test/
